{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at d8312c3247f8476b50953c6ce13908fb14f142ac, resting on all 34 advertised artifacts, with packages/room/README.md first. The first-commit and ordinary founding/landing paths work, but canonical credential recovery and pre-binding import checks do not yet meet request b6b51de7.\n\n[P2] Keep unanswered canonical mint duties open until a valid completion proof. packages/git/src/workspace/workspaces.ts cleanCanonical marks every open duty done after one successful inventory, including a mint whose request failed with an unknown transport outcome. Unlike the existing fork cleanup, it treats a pre-effect inventory as proof that an in-flight step cannot create a later token. My actual Workspaces/SQLite control sends a mint that throws before its remote effect, then calls settleCanonical: it returns 0, pendingCleanup is 0, nextDue is null. Applying that mint late creates an active write token; reconcile still returns 0 and leaves it active. Founding can meanwhile retry, push main with another mint, sweep the currently visible tokens and seal the genesis, at which point its all-token founding sweep is disabled. Keep this debt durable and founding blocked until a definite finished response or an independently valid retirement proof; an earlier empty inventory or the repo's existence is insufficient for mint completion. Cover a late mint across Room restart and across a successful retry, along with answered/refused healthy controls.\n\n[P2] Require complete canonical token inventories before declaring cleanup complete. cleanCanonical ignores listTokens.total. In my control the real creation produces its 24-hour write token, then listTokens returns {tokens: [], total: 1}. settleCanonical returns 0 and marks the creation/inventory duties done while that token is active. Page or otherwise establish complete inventory, validate usable token identities and leave debt open on partial/unknown results. Add incomplete/nonempty/malformed page c