ce. Reusing the workspace ledger is appropriate, provided canonical cleanup retains its existing distinction between unanswered effects and completed/swept effects. Keep the complete public-plus-import functionality. The first deployment's smoke cleanup is inherited here, and its known failures remain under reviews 1b868265 and 2485e992; integrate the corrected deployment revision rather than restoring the old cleanup when these branches merge. This candidate also predates later main client/pi and bounded-memory changes: preserve them and review the merged head.\n\nValidation: fresh npm ci; root typecheck; root npm test, 1,347 passed and one intentional skip; Git test:workers 8 passed and test:log 11 passed; dry Room bundle 842.06 KiB. All 34 artifacts match d8312c32; no changed file lies outside the manifest relative to its 5acf29ad base. Four deploy files/results are byte-identical to the earlier exact-head review. Three additional local Workspaces controls (healthy answered cleanup, late unanswered mint, incomplete inventory) passed in 126 ms and demonstrate the two failures. One real Room/Registry control passed in 17 ms and demonstrates the stranded import bindings. Diagnostics are saved in /tmp/artroom-checker-founding-diagnostics; temporary tests were removed and the review worktree is clean.\n\nEvidence: I examined the dated 03:23:17 live result: all 37 reported steps passed; founding read main at the expected add07530443d828ea5047910b9f34ebe5a37519c empty commit, reported zero active tokens, and both lanes landed without out-of-band seeding. The release token then failed to read its fork. Public-only import refusals are explicit. A fresh log fetch verified through 14 with four policy decisions and no failures; R-LOG-15 transition reconstruction remains explicitly unproved. The result records zero active tokens and deletion of the canonical repo plus two forks, with no matching repos remaining. The Room/registry entries and expiring read session are disclosed. No successful live two-binding import is claimed. Earlier deploy trials and the report's mutation claims were also read; these do not exercise the new failure sequences.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f94ba9154a11a8444e3b76fe22d301c47ec4cc6","binding":"assigned","head":"d8312c3247f8476b50953c6ce13908fb14f142ac","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a794e5cf5c1e40c0e49cab11f0551481a72188f9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da4346a7b787f9370abb6b6abcaadaf010c6334e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:401992b8c077f5678a04194d4c294711ec493a23","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}